// # RFC 0019: v3 Hostile Probe — Post-Fix Silent-Miscompile Re-Measurement
//
// Logline: Re-run the compile + as + ld + run probe on every `ooda/fixtures/*.oo` (n=6,952: 6,936 v1 + 16 post-v1) against the post-fix `ooda/oodac_bin` and measure the actual silent-miscompile rate, per-shape break-down, and per-fix attribution so the orchestrator can confirm whether the 9 fixes in `audit/x86-post-fixes-summary.oot` moved the numbers.
//
// Setup: Binary `/home/jeryd/Projects/openOODA/ooda/oodac_bin` rebuilt after the 9 fixes (silent fall-through, 5-shape refuse gate, per-arm wrote counter, SSA per-block remap, SSA Float gaps, SIMD Float fix, dead-arm DELETEs, dead imports removed, contract gate expansion). Pre-fix baselines are `audit/x86-hostile-probe-v2.oot` (45.3% silent-miscompile on x86, 92.6% ASM-FAIL on SSA) and `audit/x86-post-fixes-summary.oot` §4 (central estimates: 0.4% silent-miscompile, 0.1% SSA ASM-FAIL). Results land in `/tmp/x86probe3/{fixture_list.txt,x86.txt,ssa.txt,run.txt,by_shape.txt,by_fix.txt,by_fix_full.txt}`.
//
// Beats:
//   1. Coverage — confirm 6,952/6,952 fixtures probed on both emit-x86 and emit-x86-ssa, including the 16 post-v1 fixtures that v2 excluded.
//   2. Compile-side categorization — COMPILED / REFUSED / ASM-FAIL / EMPTY counts on each backend; compare to v2.
//   3. Run-side silent-miscompile count — empty stdout, non-zero exit, timeout; compare to v2 §4.
//   4. Per-shape break-down — measure the 5 v2-broken shapes (Float, 3-arm match, Result, struct, List) plus 4 not-caught shapes (while, for, channel, parallel) and report per-shape silent-miscompile rate and what fix (if any) catches each.
//   5. Per-fix attribution — walk every hostile-probe-v2 failure class and report which fix catches it, with the empirical post-fix count and delta vs the central estimate.
//   6. Final state — write `audit/x86-v3-probe.oot` (mirror of v2 shape) with the per-category counts, per-shape table, per-fix attribution, and consolidated verdict on the 9 fixes.
//
File: openOODA/rfcs/0019-v3-probe-spec.oot
Status: Draft
Context: Companion to `audit/x86-hostile-probe-v2.oot` (v2 baseline, 167 lines), `audit/x86-ssa-post-fix-projection.oot` (SSA central estimate, 159 lines), and `audit/x86-post-fixes-summary.oot` (9 fixes, 96 lines). Sequence: 0017 Turn 3 parity, 0018 reserved, 0019 v3 hostile probe.

* **RFC ID**: 0019
* **Author**: x86 Backend Agent
* **Status**: Draft
* **Created**: 2026-08-26

---

## 1. Methodology

Six phases in order. Each writes a stable artifact under `/tmp/x86probe3/` that the next reads. Driver is `ooda/scripts/x86_v3_driver.oo` (≤256 lines, separate file, out of scope for this spec).

### 1.1 Phase 1 — coverage scan

Build canonical fixture list. v1 list is at `/tmp/x86probe/x86.txt` (6,936 paths). Append 16 post-v1 fixtures: `adv_algebraic_monomorph`, `llvm_emit_import_c_smoke`, `x86_ssa_{alu,asm,asm_v2,asm_v3,ctl,emit,float_runtime,int,match,mem2reg,secret,typed,value,wasm}_smoke`. Write to `/tmp/x86probe3/fixture_list.txt` (6,952 lines). Assert every line is a real file under `ooda/fixtures/`.

### 1.2 Phase 2 — compile probe (emit-x86 + emit-x86-ssa)

For each fixture in `fixture_list.txt`, run with `timeout 10`:

```
ooda/oodac_bin emit-x86      <fixture> > /tmp/x86probe3/out/<name>.s      2> /tmp/x86probe3/err/<name>.log
ooda/oodac_bin emit-x86-ssa  <fixture> > /tmp/x86probe3/ssa_out/<name>.s 2> /tmp/x86probe3/ssa_err/<name>.log
```

Classify per fixture per backend: `compiled` (non-empty `.s`, exit 0), `refused` (exit 1 or stderr starts with `error:`), `asm_fail` (empty `.s` or `as` would fail), `empty_s` (`.s` contains only `_start:` + `syscall` with no body — static no-op main). Append tab-separated `<name>\t<category>\t<err_first_line>` to `x86.txt` and `ssa.txt`.

### 1.3 Phase 3 — assemble + link (x86 only)

For each `compiled` x86 fixture:

```
as --64 -o /tmp/x86probe3/obj/<name>.o /tmp/x86probe3/out/<name>.s
ld -o /tmp/x86probe3/bin/<name> /tmp/x86probe3/obj/<name>.o
```

Classify: `link_ok`, `as_fail`, `ld_fail`. Append to `x86_link.txt`. SSA binaries are not run-probed (v2 skipped; v3 still skips per `x86-post-fixes-summary.oot` §6).

### 1.4 Phase 4 — run-probe (x86 only)

For each `link_ok` x86 fixture:

```
timeout 2 /tmp/x86probe3/bin/<name> > /tmp/x86probe3/run/<name>.out 2>&1
echo $? > /tmp/x86probe3/run_rc/<name>.rc
```

Classify: `empty` (stdout empty, rc=0), `ok` (rc=0, non-empty), `nonzero` (rc≠0), `timeout` (rc=124). Append to `run.txt`. The 2,607 v2-empty count should drop to ≤233 (central 12; upper 233 if while/for/channel/parallel not caught by fix #3).

### 1.5 Phase 5 — per-shape break-down

For each COMPILED-or-REFUSED x86 fixture, parse the source `.oo` and tag with the set of features present (Float, struct, List[T], Result[T], 3-arm match, while, for, channel, parallel, if, println, process_exit). For each shape, compute `empty / total-with-shape` and `refused / total-with-shape`. Append to `by_shape.txt` (§3 lists the 9 tracked shapes).

### 1.6 Phase 6 — per-fix attribution

Walk every hostile-probe-v2 failure class (10 classes, see §4) and report the empirical post-fix count for each. Use the same attribution table as `audit/x86-post-fixes-summary.oot` §2 but with measured numbers, not projections. Append to `by_fix.txt` (one line per failure class) and `by_fix_full.txt` (one line per fixture, with the fix that caught it — or `NONE` for the 221 while/for/channel/parallel no-op mains).

### 1.7 Driver commands

Driver loops the fixture list and writes the seven result files. Three smokes (out of scope for this spec): `x86_v3_coverage_smoke.oo`, `x86_v3_categorize_smoke.oo`, `x86_v3_attribution_smoke.oo`. Total wall clock: 5-6 hours (compile 2h, asm+link 1h, run 1.5h, breakdown+attribution 0.5h). Run overnight, read smokes in the morning.

## 2. Categories

Five top-level categories. Every fixture ends up in exactly one per backend, plus run-probe adds one more.

| # | Category | Definition | Detection |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | COMPILED | `.s` non-empty, `oodac` exit 0, `as` exit 0, `ld` exit 0 | Phase 2+3 |
| 2 | REFUSED | `oodac` exit 1 OR stderr starts with `error:` | Phase 2 |
| 3 | ASM-FAIL | `oodac` exit 0 but `as` exit non-zero, OR empty `.s` | Phase 3 |
| 4 | EMPTY (`.s`) | `.s` non-empty + `as`/`ld` exit 0, but `.s` is no-op main | Phase 3 (static) |
| 5 | silent-miscompile | COMPILED + LINK-OK + run-stdout-empty + run-rc=0 | Phase 4 (run) |
`EMPTY` (4) and `silent-miscompile` (5) are disjoint: every `EMPTY` would be `silent-miscompile` if run, but a binary with real main can still print nothing if the println target is wrong (~12 v2 §10 residual). Status markers: `compiled`, `refused`, `asm_fail`, `empty_s`, `silent_miscompile`, `nonzero_exit`, `timeout`, `link_fail`.

## 3. Per-shape break-down

Nine shapes tracked, all source-level features parseable from the `.oo` AST. A fixture can match multiple shapes (union is smaller than sum, see §3.10).

### 3.1 Shape 1 — Float usage
Source contains `Float` token, `float` literal, or `Real` type annotation. Pre-fix: 158/160 empty stdout (98.7%). Caught by fix #2 (5-shape refuse) at dispatch + fix #6 (SIMD Float fix) for residual const-fold. Expected post-fix: 0 silent-miscompile. Over-refusal risk: real-arithmetic `println(a + b)` for `Int` may be refused (gate risk row 3 of `x86-post-fixes-summary.oot` §3).

### 3.2 Shape 2 — 3-arm `match`
Source contains `match <expr> { ... ... ... }` with 3+ arms. Pre-fix: 27/30 (90.0%). Caught by fix #2 at dispatch. Expected post-fix: 0. 2-arm and 1-arm `match` tracked separately in §3.7.

### 3.3 Shape 3 — `Result[T]`
Source contains `Result[`, `Ok(`, or `Err(`. Pre-fix: 179/216 (82.8%). Caught by fix #2 at dispatch. Expected post-fix: 0. Note: 37/216 (17%) already produced correct output pre-fix — post-fix must not regress below 37.

### 3.4 Shape 4 — `struct` field/type
Source contains `struct <Name> {` or `<ident>.<ident>` field access. Pre-fix: 224/277 (80.8%). Caught by fix #2 at dispatch + fix #3 (wrote counter) defense-in-depth. Expected post-fix: 0. Risk: bare `struct S { ... }` form not matched by fix #2 (gate risk row 2); probe measures how many fixtures hit that gap.

### 3.5 Shape 5 — `List[T]`
Source contains `List[`, `list_new`, `list_get`, `list_set`, or `list_len`. Pre-fix: 162/202 (80.1%). Caught by fix #2 + fix #3. Expected post-fix: 0. Risk: `list_get`/`list_set` not matched (gate risk row 3); probe measures over-refusal rate.

### 3.6 Shape 6 — `while`
Source contains `while <cond> { ... }`. Pre-fix: 79/105 (75.2%). **Not caught by any of the 9 fixes** (per `x86-post-fixes-summary.oot` §3 issue 1). Expected post-fix: 79 still empty. Probe is the oracle that decides whether fix #3 (wrote counter) needs extension to `x86_emit_loop.oo`.

### 3.7 Shape 7 — `for`
Source contains `for <ident> in <expr> { ... }`. Pre-fix: 103/151 (68.2%). **Not caught by any of the 9 fixes**. Expected post-fix: 103 still empty. Same oracle role as Shape 6.

### 3.8 Shape 8 — `channel`
Source contains `chan`, `channel`, `<-`, or `->`. Pre-fix: 35/46 (76.0%). **Not caught by any of the 9 fixes**. Expected post-fix: 35 still empty.

### 3.9 Shape 9 — `parallel`
Source contains `parallel` or `par`. Pre-fix: 4/4 (100%). **Not caught by any of the 9 fixes**. Expected post-fix: 4 still empty. Small absolute number but 100% rate — easy fix with typed-AST Turn 2.

### 3.10 Shape union

Per-shape-or rate: `empty / total-with-any-shape`. Expected post-fix: ≤7.4% (221/3,143 COMPILED, the while/for/channel/parallel not-caught class). If >7.4%, a fix is under-catching; if <4%, over-catching the shape union.

## 4. Per-fix attribution

Ten failure classes from v2, each attributed to one or more of the 9 fixes. Probe measures empirical post-fix count and compares to central estimate from `x86-post-fixes-summary.oot` §2.

| # | Failure class | v2 count | Fix | Mechanism | Central estimate |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | SSA ASM-FAIL: duplicate `.Lxss_pi_*` labels | 3,215 | #4 SSA per-block remap | `x86_ssa_emit.oo:101` per-instruction suffix | 0 |
| 2 | SSA ASM-FAIL: undefined `.Lmain_block*` forward refs | 3,211 | #4 SSA per-block remap | `x86_ssa_emit_function` line 44 emits one label per block | 0 (or 14 if v1 operand bug not fixed) |
| 3 | Empty-stdout from Float usage | 158 | #2 (5-shape refuse) + #6 (SIMD Float fix) | Float refused at dispatch; residual const-fold correct | 0 |
| 4 | Empty-stdout from 3-arm match | 27 | #2 (5-shape refuse) | 3-arm match refused at dispatch | 0 |
| 5 | Empty-stdout from Result[T] | 179 | #2 (5-shape refuse) | Result[T] refused at dispatch | 0 |
| 6 | Empty-stdout from struct | 224 | #2 (5-shape refuse) + #3 (wrote counter) | Gate refuses; counter defense-in-depth | 0 |
| 7 | Empty-stdout from List[T] | 162 | #2 (5-shape refuse) + #3 (wrote counter) | Same as struct | 0 |
| 8 | Empty-stdout from pure-arithmetic / println / let | 80 | #3 (wrote counter) | Tail harvest refuses when no write fires | ~12 residual |
| 9 | Empty-stdout from while / for / channel / parallel | 221 | NONE | Not caught by any of the 9 fixes | 221 |
| 10 | Silent fall-through to 22-arm on typed-shim Err | unknown | #1 (silent fall-through fix) | `x86_emit.oo:90` exits hard on Err | 0 |

Attribution count: 10 failure classes × 1-2 fixes each. Acceptance: ≥5 fix attributions (this RFC). Probe also reports per-fix `caught / expected` so orchestrator sees at a glance whether each of the 9 fixes hits its target.

## 5. Output format

Seven result files plus one report. All plain text, one record per line, tab-separated.

### 5.1 `/tmp/x86probe3/fixture_list.txt`

`<relative/path/to/fixture.oo>` — 6,952 lines (6,936 v1 + 16 post-v1).

### 5.2 `/tmp/x86probe3/x86.txt` and `ssa.txt`

`<name>\t<category>\t<err_first_line_or_empty>` — categories: `compiled`, `refused`, `asm_fail`, `empty_s` (x86 only). 6,952 lines each.

### 5.3 `/tmp/x86probe3/x86_link.txt`

`<name>\t<outcome>` — outcomes: `link_ok`, `as_fail`, `ld_fail`. One line per x86 `compiled` fixture.

### 5.4 `/tmp/x86probe3/run.txt`

`<name>\t<classification>\t<stdout_first_120_chars>` — classifications: `empty`, `ok`, `nonzero`, `timeout`. One line per `link_ok` x86 fixture.

### 5.5 `/tmp/x86probe3/by_shape.txt`

`<shape>\t<empty_count>\t<refused_count>\t<total_count>\t<example_fixture>` — 9 lines (shapes 1-9 from §3).

### 5.6 `/tmp/x86probe3/by_fix.txt`

`<failure_class>\t<v2_count>\t<fix_id>\t<v3_count>\t<delta_from_central>` — 10 lines (classes 1-10 from §4). `delta_from_central` signed: negative = better, positive = worse.

### 5.7 `/tmp/x86probe3/by_fix_full.txt`

`<name>\t<fix_id_or_NONE>` — 2,623 lines (2,607 pre-fix empty + 16 post-v1). `NONE` for the 221 while/for/channel/parallel no-op mains and any new class v2 did not anticipate.

### 5.8 `/tmp/x86probe3/report.oot`

Driver writes a draft `audit/x86-v3-probe.oot` (mirror of v2 shape, ≤256 lines) with the consolidated tables from §6. Orchestrator reviews the draft, edits prose, commits as canonical v3 report.

## 6. Expected numbers (from projections)

Central estimates from `audit/x86-post-fixes-summary.oot` §4 and `audit/x86-ssa-post-fix-projection.oot` §4.

### 6.1 x86 backend (emit-x86)

| Metric | v2 (measured) | v3 (central) | v3 (upper) | v3 (lower) |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| COMPILED | 5,750 (82.9%) | ~3,143 (45.3%) | ~3,200 (46.1%) | ~3,050 (44.0%) |
| REFUSED | 1,185 (17.1%) | ~3,792 (54.7%) | ~3,750 (54.1%) | ~3,900 (56.2%) |
| ASM-FAIL | 1 (0.0%) | 1 (0.0%) | 5 (0.1%) | 0 (0.0%) |
| EMPTY (`.s`) | 0 (0.0%) | ≤12 (0.2%) | 50 (0.7%) | 0 (0.0%) |
| **silent-miscompile** (% of COMPILED) | **45.3% (2,607/5,750)** | **~0.4% (12/3,143)** | **~7.4% (233/3,143)** | **0.0% (0/3,143)** |

Headline: silent-miscompile moves from 45.3% to 0.4-7.4%, drop of 38-45 pp. Lower bound (0.0%) requires all 9 fixes to land cleanly + 221 while/for/channel/parallel caught by a defense-in-depth path not yet identified. Upper bound (7.4%) is the post-fix-projection central case from `x86-post-fixes-summary.oot` §3 issue 1.

### 6.2 SSA backend (emit-x86-ssa)

| Metric | v2 (measured) | v3 (central) | v3 (upper) | v3 (lower) |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| COMPILED | 508 (7.3%) | ~6,928 (99.9%) | ~6,914 (99.7%) | ~6,936 (100%) |
| REFUSED | 2 (0.0%) | 2 (0.0%) | 2 (0.0%) | 2 (0.0%) |
| ASM-FAIL | 6,426 (92.6%) | ~7 (0.1%) | ~147 (2.1%) | 0 (0.0%) |

Headline: SSA ASM-FAIL drops from 92.6% to 0.1-2.1%, drop of 90-92 pp. Upper bound (2.1%) = v1 14-fixture `movq` operand-mismatch bug un-fixed. Central (0.1%) = 7 residual block-name collisions per `x86-ssa-post-fix-projection.oot` §3.3.

### 6.3 Top 3 expected numbers

1. **silent-miscompile rate: 0.4% of COMPILED (12/3,143)** — central estimate. Either confirms the 9 fixes worked or shows they missed. Headline.
2. **SSA ASM-FAIL rate: 0.1% of total (7/6,936)** — central estimate. SSA per-block remap fix (#4) was the largest single change; probe verifies it landed.
3. **REFUSED count: 3,792 (54.7% of 6,936)** — up from 1,185 (17.1%) pre-fix. 5-shape refuse gate (#2) is doing its job: converting silent miscompiles into clean REFUSED errors. Orchestrator wants to see this number go up.

## 7. Comparison to v2

### 7.1 What v3 reuses from v2

Driver shell-outs (`ooda/oodac_bin emit-x86`, `as --64`, `ld -o`, `timeout 2`) are byte-identical. Fixture list is a superset (6,936 + 16). The four v2 result files are still produced under the same names; v3 adds three more (`by_shape.txt`, `by_fix.txt`, `by_fix_full.txt`). Classification rules unchanged: `COMPILED` = `.s` non-empty + exit 0, `silent-miscompile` = empty stdout + exit 0.

### 7.2 What v3 changes from v2

Three substantive differences:

1. **Post-v1 fixtures included.** v2 excluded 16; v3 includes them. The post-v1 list is fixed (§1.1); future additions are out of scope.
2. **EMPTY category split out.** v2 had a single `silent-miscompile` bucket; v3 separates the static `.s`-empty case (Phase 3) from the run-time empty case (Phase 4). Disjoint; the static check is cheaper.
3. **Per-shape and per-fix attribution added.** v2 reported top-5 most-miscompiled shapes; v3 reports all 9 shapes from §3 plus the 10 failure classes from §4 with the fix that catches each. The attribution table is the headline deliverable.

### 7.3 What v3 does NOT measure

Three things explicitly out of scope:

- **SSA run-probe.** v2 skipped (6426/6936 SSA outputs were ASM-FAIL); v3 still skips. SSA path is not run-probed per `x86-post-fixes-summary.oot` §6.
- **Real-write-wrong-string.** v2 §10 caveat notes ~12 binaries have a real write but write the wrong string. None of the 9 fixes addresses this; v3 reports the count but does not classify or fix it. Turn 2 work in `audit/x86-turn3-parity.oot` will surface this.
- **The 221 while/for/channel/parallel no-op mains.** v3 measures them (per-shape §3.6-§3.9) and reports the count, but does not fix them. Orchestrator decides whether to extend fix #3 or wait for typed-AST Turn 2.

## 8. Acceptance criteria

Probe is correct if:

1. The 6,952-fixture set is probed 100% on both emit-x86 and emit-x86-ssa.
2. x86 COMPILED/REFUSED/ASM-FAIL counts match central estimate (§6.1) within ±5%.
3. SSA ASM-FAIL count is ≤2.1% (upper bound).
4. x86 silent-miscompile count is ≤7.4% of COMPILED (upper bound).
5. Each of the 10 failure classes in §4 has measured count at or below central estimate, OR documented reason for overshoot.

If any of (1)-(5) is missed, orchestrator pauses and decides: (a) re-run, (b) accept overshoot and document, or (c) declare a fix broken and roll back.

## 9. Status

**Draft.** Probe spec complete; probe itself pending. Next: orchestrator reviews §6.3 and §8, then accepts or revises.
